<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35644" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνθῡμ-ημᾰτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>determined, resolute,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Decent.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>skilled in the use of enthymemes,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1354b22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>consisting of</i> or <i>in the form of enthymemes,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥητορεῖαι</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				1356b21
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θόρυβοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Nat.</u>
					14.9
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερον, [σχῆμα</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Corn.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				p.397
			</span></i> H. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1418b36
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Theon
				<u>Prog.</u>
				5
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
